@startuml E3_API_05_LAYERED
title API 05: Portfolio, Backtesting and Risk APIs (LAYERED view)
!theme plain
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 80
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle


' REST interfaces are grounded in the Express/FastAPI route declarations.
' Layered and MVC are two views of the existing CryptoWeb codebase, not separate implementations.
actor "React client / admin" as Client

component "Server_3 :4000 - Portfolio\nGET /api/portfolio" as API1 <<REST API>>
component "Server_3 :4000 - Backtest\nPOST /api/backtest\nGET /api/backtest" as API2 <<REST API>>
component "Server_3 :4000 - Risk analytics\nGET /api/portfolio/risk/news\nGET /api/portfolio/risk/summary\nGET /api/portfolio/risk/scenarios\nGET /api/portfolio/risk/correlation\nGET /api/portfolio/risk/propagation" as API3 <<REST API>>

package "Routing and controller layer" {
  component "portfolio.controller.js\nbacktest.controller.js\nportfolioRisk.controller.js" as Controllers <<Controllers / route handlers>>
}
package "Service and orchestration layer" {
  component "livePrice.service.js\nportfolioRisk.service.js\ncorrelation.service.js" as Services <<Services / jobs>>
}
database "MongoDB: trades, backtest, candle, news" as Storage
Client --> API1 : HTTP / JSON
Client --> API2 : HTTP / JSON
Client --> API3 : HTTP / JSON
API1 --> Controllers : dispatch
API2 --> Controllers : dispatch
API3 --> Controllers : dispatch
Controllers --> Services : calls
Services --> Storage : reads/writes


note bottom of Storage
  Database objects summarized by domain;
  this is an API interaction diagram,
  not a physical ER diagram.
end note
@enduml
